# The apps tier: the rest of upstream's omarchy-base.packages that exists for
# aarch64 and is not needed to bring the session up, less the eight
# vm/packages/omitted leaves out on purpose, plus GNOME's phone apps at the end.
#
# Installed by default, because "get it running as Omarchy is" means Omarchy's
# applications and not just its compositor. Skipped by
# `./scripts/vm-build.sh --session-only`, which is the flag to reach for while
# iterating on the session: none of it decides whether Hyprland starts.
#
# The browser is the one place this tier contradicts upstream outright, and
# vm/packages/omitted carries the measurements. Chromium has no narrow layout:
# at the 360px panel its own first-run dialog is clipped off the right edge
# with no reachable button, and behind that it never maps a browser window at
# all -- `ContextResult::kTransientFailure: Failed to send
# GpuControl.CreateCommandBuffer`, the same missing hardware EGL that makes mpv
# abort below. Epiphany reflows to a phone layout on its own, with the URL bar
# and the back/forward/tabs row moved to the bottom of the screen where a thumb
# reaches them.
#
# It is also the cheapest package in this file. Every one of epiphany's 23
# dependencies is already installed -- webkitgtk-6.0, gtk4 and libadwaita came
# in for Calendar, Contacts and Geary -- so `pacman -S epiphany` on the built
# image pulls in nothing else: 3.59 MiB of download against chromium's 117.28,
# and 17.59 MiB installed against 434.36.
epiphany
