# --- GNOME's phone apps ---------------------------------------------------
# Not upstream's: Omarchy is a desktop and leaves calendars, contacts and maps
# to a browser tab. A phone without them is missing what a phone is for, the
# reason [pkg.moarchy-keep] gives for Notes. All are libadwaita, so they reflow
# to the 360px panel, and all are in ALARM's aarch64 [extra].
#
# Each fills a gap rather than doubling a tile. nautilus, foot and imv stay
# upstream's handlers, and so does mpv, which upstream's screen recorder
# and yt-dlp host also run. Its tile is what changes: in the VM mpv aborts at
# startup (no hardware EGL, then an assertion in its X11 fallback), so the
# drawer's player is Showtime, and mpv's entry is hidden by a copy of it in
# default/etc/skel/.local/share/applications. Audio is Amberol's, which claims the
# audio types mpv claims, so audio/mpeg opens in Amberol -- the point being that
# mpv is the one that does not start here. Geary is the mail client that upstream's aether would have been
# (omitted: x86_64-only). Camera is for the phone this image stands in for; the
# VM has no /dev/video, so there it stops at the portal's permission prompt.
#
# About 135 MB of download, against the 400 MB the six omitted packages cost.
# Most of it is two WebKits that evolution-data-server brings for Calendar and
# Contacts, and Geary uses webkit2gtk-4.1 too, so it costs only 3 MB more.
# Camera, Amberol and Sound Recorder share their GStreamer plugins, and Showtime
# plays through the same ones; Amberol is 1.9 MB of that.
#
# Amberol and not GNOME Music, measured at the 360x674 panel on 2026-09-12.
# Music has no narrow layout: no AdwBreakpoint anywhere in its UI files, a 220px
# playlist sidebar and a 250px volume slider, so at 360 the window is laid out
# wider than the surface it was given and the overflow is cut -- its welcome
# text ends mid-word. That is not a label bug, and a label fix does not touch
# it: adding wrap and a 30-character cap to those labels, rebuilding Music's
# gresource and restarting it changed nothing, while the same widgets built
# standalone in a 360px window wrap at 336px. Upstream tracks the window itself
# as gnome-music#255. Amberol is GNOME Circle rather than core GNOME -- adaptive
# is a rule of that programme -- and it renders correctly at this size. It costs
# 1.9 MB where Music cost 7.4, and runs no localsearch indexer behind it.
gnome-calculator
gnome-calendar
gnome-contacts
gnome-maps
gnome-clocks
gnome-weather
gnome-text-editor
geary
snapshot
amberol
gnome-sound-recorder
showtime

